  "level": 4,
  "order": 401,
  "theme": "home",
  "culturalNote": "Many Nairobi homes have a small garden — a \"bustani\" for flowers, or a \"shamba\" for vegetables like sukuma and spinach — and an older gardener who knows every plant by name. Address an older man respectfully as \"mzee\". Kupanda means both \"to plant\" and \"to climb / get on\" (a matatu); context tells you which. A \"fundi\" is anyone skilled with their hands, and calling someone \"fundi kweli\" (a real fundi) is high praise.",
  "startingPoint": "Saturday morning. Mzee Ochieng, who looks after the garden of your block, is already at work with a hoe.",
  "grammarFocus": [
    "present-na",
